cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use HiBench Next in your research, please cite this software."

type: software

title: "HiBench Next: A Heterogeneous Benchmark Suite for Modern Apache Spark"

authors:
  - family-names: Garralda-Barrio
    given-names: Mariano
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0008-0201-2984

version: "2.5.0"

repository-code: "https://github.com/mgarralda/HiBench-Next"

license: Apache-2.0

keywords:
  - HiBench
  - Apache Spark
  - Spark benchmarking
  - distributed computing
  - DataFrames
  - Spark ML
  - Spark SQL
  - performance evaluation
  - research software
  - workload diversity

abstract: >
  HiBench Next is a reengineering of Intel's HiBench benchmark suite
  for modern Apache Spark batch workloads. It provides Spark structured
  API implementations, Spark-based data generators with configurable
  seeds and scale parameters, and workload-specific input formats.
  The software integrates a web interface, REST API, persistent
  experiment configurations, execution management, and historical
  reporting, Scala and PySpark workload implementations, and comparative
  analysis with downloadable evidence. It supports controlled experiments across heterogeneous
  Spark workloads. The scope of implementation and experimental
  validation is documented in the repository.
